---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Circular Justice" description="Circular Justice is a discovery-stage social-innovation concept exploring more circular institutional material flows.">
  <section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Discovery-stage social-innovation concept</p><h1>Circular Justice</h1><p class="lead">Circular Justice is a discovery-stage social-innovation concept examining whether institutional material flows can be managed more circularly — reducing avoidable waste while exploring responsible opportunities for reuse, skills development, training and rehabilitation.</p></section>
  <section class="grid"><article class="card"><h2>What we are exploring</h2><p>Institutional waste measurement, reduction, reuse and recycling opportunities, and the practical conditions needed to evaluate them responsibly.</p></article><article class="card"><h2>Potential social value</h2><p>Where appropriate and subject to safeguards, the concept considers green skills, rehabilitation and credible employment pathways.</p></article><article class="card"><h2>What we are seeking</h2><p>Research, operational and technology partners able to challenge the discovery question, methods, safeguards and evidence requirements.</p></article></section>
  <section class="statement"><h2>Responsible development</h2><p>Early work may use synthetic, aggregated or appropriately authorised data. The proposed platform would not make automated decisions about individual prisoners. Any future institutional work would require appropriate safeguards, human review and formal permissions.</p></section>
  <section class="clarification"><h2>Current status</h2><p>The concept is not yet an operating programme and no institutional partnership, savings, environmental outcome or participant benefit is claimed in advance. Its purpose at this stage is to investigate whether a safe, measurable and transferable model can be developed. Circular Justice is not a live AI platform. It has no prison or HMPPS partnership, no access to prisoners or prisoner data, no approved government pilot, no established European consortium and no funding approval.</p></section>
  <p class="contact"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Discuss research or partnership fit</a></p>
  <style>.hero{max-width:88ch;padding:8px 0 18px}.eyebrow{color:#0f766e;font-size:13px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 9px}h1{margin:0 0 10px;font-size:clamp(40px,6vw,60px);color:var(--text);letter-spacing:-.03em}h2{margin:0 0 9px;color:var(--text);font-size:19px}.lead,p{color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75}.lead{font-size:19px;margin:0}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px;margin-top:14px}.card,.statement,.clarification{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:18px;background:white;box-shadow:0 6px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.05)}.card p,.statement p,.clarification p{margin:0}.statement{margin-top:14px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.06),rgba(16,185,129,.07))}.clarification{margin-top:14px}.contact{margin-top:18px}.btn{display:inline-flex;padding:11px 14px;border:1px solid rgba(37,99,235,.25);border-radius:14px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.10),rgba(16,185,129,.10));color:var(--text);text-decoration:none;font-weight:800}@media(max-width:800px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
</BaseLayout>
